# Court Metrics 1877-2026 - Future Law Predictor

https://claude.ai/public/artifacts/a3a964c6-b55b-43fc-94df-ab85168fa60c

Used a database of 184k decisions across 14 Canadian courts. Data includes court, party names, dates, word/sentence counts, reading-grade level, and an in-document citation count, but no opinion text. This research reads **litigant names and cross-court movement** as the signal.

Interesting notes:
- **Platform arbitration clauses** — *Uber v. Heller* (2020 SCC) struck one down as unconscionable; Amazon has since been hit with the same theory in three separate suits still working through FC/FCA.
- **Cross-border privacy claims** — *Douez v. Facebook* ran for **12 years** across 10 rulings and still wasn't fully resolved after the SCC weighed in; six different plaintiffs sued Google in BC alone since 2020 with no consolidating ruling.
- **Crypto exchange jurisdiction** — first appellate rulings only arrived in 2024-2025 (*Binance v. OSC*, *Coinbase*).
- **Microsoft licensing disputes** — included as a settled/declining contrast card, same as the Bykovets card in the SCC version.

Note: without opinion text, "unsettled" here means **procedural churn** (same dispute bouncing across courts, or many plaintiffs suing the same platform with no unifying ruling) — not a verified doctrinal split the way the text-based SCC analysis could show. 
